IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 48 to 49 and Schedule 1: rules of court, and the savings and transitional provisions.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- s 49 is shown only as a row of dots and is not encoded.
-- Schedule 1 speaks of the commencement of sections of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 and of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985.
-- The text gives no commencement day for any of them, so every rule below takes the day as an input, and the days in the tests are fixtures chosen for the tests:
-- 1 January 1982 for the sections of the 1981 Act and 1 July 1986 for the sections of the 1985 Act.
-- "After the commencement" is read as on or after the day of the commencement, because a provision that commences on a day takes effect at the first moment of that day (s 9(5)).

§ `s 48: rules of court`

-- src:1245 | rules of court, used in relation to any Court, shall mean rules made by the authority having, for the time being, power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of such court.
@ref s 48(1) (src:1245)
GIVEN `the rules are made by the authority having, for the time being, power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(1): the rules are rules of court` `the rules are made by the authority having, for the time being, power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court` MEANS
    `the rules are made by the authority having, for the time being, power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court`

-- src:1247 | (2) The power of such authority to make rules of court shall include power to make rules of court for the purposes of any Act which directs or authorizes anything to be done by rules of court.
@ref s 48(2) (src:1247)
GIVEN `the authority has power to make rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act directs or authorizes the thing to be done by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2): the power includes power to make rules of court for the purposes of the Act` `the authority has power to make rules of court` `an Act directs or authorizes the thing to be done by rules of court` MEANS
    IF `the authority has power to make rules of court` AND `an Act directs or authorizes the thing to be done by rules of court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 48(1): the rules are rules of court` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 48(1): the rules are rules of court` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 48(2): the power includes power to make rules of court for the purposes of the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(2): the power includes power to make rules of court for the purposes of the Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(2): the power includes power to make rules of court for the purposes of the Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 48A: savings and transitional provisions`

-- src:1249 | 48A. Savings and transitional provisions
-- src:1251 | Schedule 1 has effect.
@ref s 48A (src:1249-1251)
`s 48A: Schedule 1 has effect` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 48A: Schedule 1 has effect`

§ `Schedule 1: the helper used by most clauses`

-- "In operation at the commencement, or comes into operation after it": a thing is within the clause unless it ceased to operate before the commencement day.
GIVEN `the day the amending provision commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the thing came into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day the thing ceased to be in operation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the amending provision commenced` `the day the thing came into operation` `the day the thing ceased to be in operation` MEANS
    IF `the day the thing came into operation` GREATER THAN `the day the amending provision commenced`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the thing ceased to be in operation`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST ended THEN ended AT LEAST `the day the amending provision commenced`

#ASSERT `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` (Date 1 1 1982) (Date 1 1 1970) NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` (Date 1 1 1982) (Date 1 1 1970) (JUST (Date 1 1 1982))
#ASSERT `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` (Date 1 1 1982) (Date 1 1 1982) NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` (Date 1 1 1982) (Date 2 1 1982) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` (Date 1 1 1982) (Date 1 1 1970) (JUST (Date 31 12 1981)))

§ `Schedule 1, clauses 1 to 4: sections 4, 5, 7 and 7A`

-- src:1259 | 1. Savings and transitional – section 4
-- src:1261 | Section 4 as amended by section 4 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies in the interpretation and construction of regulations that –
-- src:1263 | (a) are in operation at the commencement of the lastmentioned section; or
-- src:1265 | (b) take effect after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 1 (src:1259-1265)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations came into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations ceased to be in operation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 1: section 4 as amended applies in the interpretation and construction of the regulations` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the regulations came into operation` `the day the regulations ceased to be in operation` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the regulations came into operation` `the day the regulations ceased to be in operation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1267 | 2. Savings and transitional – section 5
-- src:1269 | Section 5 as amended by section 5 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies to a reference to an Act that –
-- src:1271 | (a) is in operation at the commencement of the lastmentioned section; or
-- src:1273 | (b) comes into operation at that commencement –
-- src:1275 | and whether the reference is contained in an Act passed before or after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 2 (src:1267-1275)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act referred to came into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act referred to ceased to be in operation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 2: section 5 as amended applies to the reference to the Act` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act referred to came into operation` `the day the Act referred to ceased to be in operation` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act referred to came into operation` `the day the Act referred to ceased to be in operation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1277 | 3. Savings and transitional – section 7
-- src:1279 | Section 7 as substituted by section 6 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies to a reference to the expression "prescribed" where the expression appears in an Act –
-- src:1281 | (a) passed before and in force at the commencement of the lastmentioned section; or
-- src:1283 | (b) passed after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 3 (src:1277-1283)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act in which the expression appears was passed` IS A DATE
      `the Act in which the expression appears is in force at that commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 3: section 7 as substituted applies to the reference to the expression prescribed` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act in which the expression appears was passed` `the Act in which the expression appears is in force at that commencement` MEANS
    IF `the day the Act in which the expression appears was passed` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced`
       OR (`the day the Act in which the expression appears was passed` BELOW `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` AND `the Act in which the expression appears is in force at that commencement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "where"

-- src:1285 | 4. Savings and transitional – section 7A
-- src:1287 | Section 7A as substituted by section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies to and in relation to an Act that –
-- src:1289 | (a) is in operation at the commencement of the lastmentioned section; or
-- src:1291 | (b) comes into operation after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 4 (src:1285-1291)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act came into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act ceased to be in operation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 4: section 7A as substituted applies to and in relation to the Act` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act came into operation` `the day the Act ceased to be in operation` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act came into operation` `the day the Act ceased to be in operation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

