§ `Schedule 1, clauses 5 to 7: sections 11, 13 and 16`

-- Clause 5 joins its two limbs with "and", yet limb (a) needs an Act passed after the commencement and limb (b) an Act passed before it, so both cannot hold.
-- The rule below reads the "and" as "or", as every sibling clause does; the next rule is the clause as printed and is never true.
-- src:1293 | 5. Savings and transitional – section 11
-- src:1295 | A power conferred by section 11, as substituted by section 9 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981, the exercise of which is dependent on the existence of a provision of a kind referred to in section 11 (1) or, as the case may be, first referred to in section 11 (2), is exercisable where the Act in which the provision is contained –
-- src:1297 | (a) is passed after the commencement of section 9 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981; and
-- src:1299 | (b) was passed before that commencement but the provision had not come into operation before that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 5 (src:1293-1299)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` IS A DATE
      `the provision had come into operation before that commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 5: the power conferred by section 11 as substituted is exercisable` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` `the provision had come into operation before that commencement` MEANS
    IF `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced`
       OR (`the day the Act containing the provision was passed` BELOW `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` AND (NOT (`the provision had come into operation before that commencement`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "where"

@ref Schedule 1 clause 5 as printed (src:1293-1299)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` IS A DATE
      `the provision had come into operation before that commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 5 as printed: limbs (a) and (b) both hold` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` `the provision had come into operation before that commencement` MEANS
    `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced`
    AND `the day the Act containing the provision was passed` BELOW `the day the lastmentioned section commenced`
    AND (NOT (`the provision had come into operation before that commencement`))

-- src:1301 | 6. Savings and transitional – section 13
-- src:1303 | Section 13 as amended by section 11 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 –
-- src:1305 | (a) applies to a reference to an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act that –
-- src:1307 | (i) is in operation at the commencement of the lastmentioned section; or
-- src:1309 | (ii) comes into operation after that commencement –
-- src:1311 | and whether the reference is contained in an Act passed before or after that commencement; and
-- src:1313 | (b) applies, in the case of a reference contained in an Act that came into operation before the commencement of the lastmentioned section, whether or not the reference is followed by words indicating that the reference includes subsequent amendments of the Imperial or Commonwealth Act referred to.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 6 (src:1301-1313)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act referred to came into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act referred to ceased to be in operation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 6(a): section 13 as amended applies to the reference to the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act referred to came into operation` `the day the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act referred to ceased to be in operation` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act referred to came into operation` `the day the Imperial Act or Commonwealth Act referred to ceased to be in operation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the Act containing the reference came into operation before the commencement of the lastmentioned section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is followed by words indicating that it includes subsequent amendments of the Imperial or Commonwealth Act referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 6(b): section 13 as amended applies to the reference, whether or not it is followed by words about subsequent amendments` `the Act containing the reference came into operation before the commencement of the lastmentioned section` `the reference is followed by words indicating that it includes subsequent amendments of the Imperial or Commonwealth Act referred to` MEANS
    IF `the Act containing the reference came into operation before the commencement of the lastmentioned section` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thing that section 16 as amended applies to` IS ONE OF
    `an Act`
    `regulations`
    `any other instrument or document`

-- src:1315 | 7. Savings and transitional – section 16
-- src:1317 | Section 16 as amended by section 12 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies only –
-- src:1319 | (a) to an Act, whether passed before or after the commencement of the lastmentioned section, which expires after that commencement; and
-- src:1321 | (b) to regulations, whether made before or after that commencement, which are rescinded, expire or cease to have effect after that commencement; and
-- src:1323 | (c) to any other instrument or document, whether made before or after that commencement, which expires or ceases to have effect after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 7 (src:1315-1323)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      thing IS A `Thing that section 16 as amended applies to`
      `the day it expired, was rescinded or ceased to have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 7: section 16 as amended applies to the thing` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` thing `the day it expired, was rescinded or ceased to have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act` THEN IF `the day it expired, was rescinded or ceased to have effect` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `regulations` THEN IF `the day it expired, was rescinded or ceased to have effect` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other instrument or document` THEN IF `the day it expired, was rescinded or ceased to have effect` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

