§ `Schedule 1, clauses 12 to 16: sections 38A, 39A, 40A, 46 and 47`

-- src:1359 | 12. Savings and transitional – section 38A
-- src:1361 | (1) Section 38A as substituted by section 18 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies to a proclamation or an order-in-council that –
-- src:1363 | (a) is made after the commencement of the lastmentioned section; or
-- src:1365 | (b) has been made before that commencement but has not taken effect before that commencement –
-- src:1367 | and, where made under an Act or Imperial Act, so applies whether the Act or Imperial Act was passed before or after that commencement.
-- src:1369 | (2) Section 38A as substituted by section 6 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985 applies to any proclamation or order-in-council or to a prescribed instrument within the meaning of section 38A that –
-- src:1371 | (a) is made after the commencement of section 6 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985; or
-- src:1373 | (b) has been made before that commencement but has not taken effect before that commencement –
-- src:1375 | and, in the case of –
-- src:1377 | (c) a proclamation or order-in-council was made under an Act or Imperial Act, so applies, whether the Act or Imperial Act was passed before or after that commencement; or
-- src:1379 | (d) a prescribed instrument, so applies, whether the Act under which the instrument is made was passed before or after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 12 (src:1359-1379)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the proclamation, order-in-council or prescribed instrument was made` IS A DATE
      `the day it took effect` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 12: section 38A as substituted applies to the proclamation, order-in-council or prescribed instrument` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the proclamation, order-in-council or prescribed instrument was made` `the day it took effect` MEANS
    IF `the day the proclamation, order-in-council or prescribed instrument was made` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day it took effect`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST effective THEN IF effective AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1381 | 13. Savings and transitional – section 39A
-- src:1383 | Section 39A as inserted by section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985 applies to regulations referred to in subsection (1) of section 39A that –
-- src:1385 | (a) are in force at the commencement of section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985; or
-- src:1387 | (b) come into force after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 13 (src:1381-1387)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations came into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations ceased to be in force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 13: section 39A as inserted applies to the regulations referred to in subsection (1) of section 39A` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the regulations came into force` `the day the regulations ceased to be in force` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the regulations came into force` `the day the regulations ceased to be in force` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1389 | 14. Savings and transitional – section 40A
-- src:1391 | Section 40A as inserted by section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985 applies to a reference in an Act within the meaning of section 40A that –
-- src:1393 | (a) is in operation at the commencement of section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985; or
-- src:1395 | (b) comes into operation after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 14 (src:1389-1395)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act containing the reference came into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act containing the reference ceased to be in operation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 14: section 40A as inserted applies to the reference in the Act` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act containing the reference came into operation` `the day the Act containing the reference ceased to be in operation` MEANS
    IF `Schedule 1: the thing was in operation at the commencement, or came into operation after it` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act containing the reference came into operation` `the day the Act containing the reference ceased to be in operation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1397 | 15. Savings and transitional – section 46
-- src:1399 | Section 46 as amended by section 20 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies to and in relation to the interpretation and construction of the expression "offence" whether the Act in which that expression occurs was passed before or after the commencement of the lastmentioned section.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 15 (src:1397-1399)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act in which the expression occurs was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 15: section 46 as amended applies to and in relation to the expression offence` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the Act in which the expression occurs was passed` MEANS
    IF `the day the Act in which the expression occurs was passed` BELOW `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` OR `the day the Act in which the expression occurs was passed` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1401 | 16. Savings and transitional – section 47
-- src:1403 | (1) Section 47 as amended by section 21 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 applies to regulations made after the commencement of the lastmentioned section and so applies whether the Act under which they are made was passed before or after that commencement, and section 47 (as in force before that commencement) continues to apply to regulations made before that commencement as if section 21 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 had not been enacted.
-- src:1405 | (2) Section 47 as amended by section 9 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1985 applies to regulations made after the commencement of the lastmentioned section and so applies whether the Act under which they are made was passed before or after that commencement.
@ref Schedule 1 clause 16(1) (src:1401-1405)
GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations were made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 16(1): section 47 as amended applies to the regulations` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the regulations were made` MEANS
    IF `the day the regulations were made` AT LEAST `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations were made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 16(1): section 47 as in force before that commencement continues to apply to the regulations` `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` `the day the regulations were made` MEANS
    IF `the day the regulations were made` BELOW `the day the lastmentioned section commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

